description: Documentation standards for docs and READMEs
globs: "**/*.md,docs/**"
alwaysApply: false
---
# Documentation
- **When**: document a change when behaviour, contracts, setup or architecture changed. No docs
  written for the sake of file count.
- **Where**:
  - feature docs in `docs/features/<feature>.md`;
  - decisions in `.agent/memory/decisions/`;
  - API contracts next to the code (OpenAPI/XML docs).
- **Content**: one source of truth per fact. Link to it instead of copying.
- **Style**: lead with purpose, keep it short, use present tense, and write commands as copyable
  code blocks.
- **Accuracy**: verify every command, path and name you write against the repo.
